Types of Variables in UiPath

Text Variables (String)
 Text variables are used to store text values such as names, messages, and addresses.

True/False Variables (Boolean)
 Boolean variables are used to store logical values, either True or False.

Number Variables (Integer/Double)
 Number variables are used to store numeric values such as integers and decimal numbers.

Array Variables
 Array variables are used to store a collection of values of the same data type, such as multiple integers or strings.

Date and Time Variables (DateTime)
 Date and Time variables are used to store date and time information.

Data Table Variables (DataTable)
 Data Table variables are used to store data in a tabular format consisting of rows and columns.

Generic Variables (Object)
 Generic variables are used to store different types of data when the exact data type is not known in advance.
 ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

 Properties of a Variable in UiPath
1. Name

The Name property specifies the identifier used to refer to the variable throughout the workflow.

Example:

Plain Text
employeeName
totalAmount
currentDate
2. Data Type

The Data Type property defines the kind of data that the variable can store.

Examples:

Data Type	Stores
String	Text values
Int32	Whole numbers
Boolean	True/False values
DateTime	Date and time values
DataTable	Tabular data
Array	Collection of values

Example:

Plain Text
employeeName → String
age → Int32
isValid → Boolean
3. Scope

The Scope property determines where the variable can be accessed within the workflow.

Example:

Scope = Main → Variable can be used throughout the Main workflow.
Scope = Sequence1 → Variable can be used only inside Sequence1.

Think of Scope as the visibility area of a variable.

4. Default Value

The Default Value property assigns an initial value to the variable when it is created.

Examples:

Plain Text
employeeName = "Harini"
age = 20
isValid = True
currentDate = 20/12/2026

If no default value is provided, UiPath assigns a default value based on the data type (e.g., 0 for numbers, False for Boolean, Nothing for String).
